<title>USA: Mining Services Q3 net, share higher.</title>
<headline>Mining Services Q3 net, share higher.</headline>
<dateline>SALT LAKE CITY 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>(unaudited)</p>
<p>						Three Months Ended</p>
<p>					     Sep 30,	     Sep 30,</p>
<p>						  1996		 1995</p>
<p> Revenue(a)			   $7,121,000	  $5,936,000</p>
<p> Income before taxes		 1,829,000	   1,241,000</p>
<p> Net income			    1,352,000	     865,000</p>
<p> Net income per share		  0.21(b)	     0.15(c)</p>
<p> Fully diluted shares		6,385,027	   5,819,260</p>
<p>						 Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>					     Sep 30,	     Sep 30,</p>
<p>						 1996		  1995</p>
<p> Revenue(a)			   18,917,000	  17,637,000</p>
<p> Income before taxes		 4,100,000	   2,791,000</p>
<p> Net income			    3,066,000	   1,959,000</p>
<p> Net income per share		  0.48(b)	     0.34(c)</p>
<p> Fully diluted shares		6,385,027	   5,819,260</p>
<p>(a) Revenue consists of net sales, royalties and equity in earnings of nonconsolidated joint ventures. (b) Primary earnings per share for the first three and nine months of 1996 were $0.21 and $0.49 per share, respectively. (c) Earnings per share for the first three and nine months of 1995 restated based on current fully diluted shares of 6,385,027 shares were $0.14 and $0.31, respectively. NOTE:  On Sept. 4, 1996, the company released a news bulletin indicating that a 10 percent stock dividend was declared.  The characterization of the stock distribution was intended to be that of a stock split which was issued on Oct. 18, 1996 to stockholder's of record on Sept. 18, 1996.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
